1. [BLOCKER] bootstrap/compiler.rb:1076 — `is_expression_start` omits `nothing` (and `mightfail`) while src/parser.rs:1778 counts `Nothing`/`MightFail` as expression starts, so `xs at nothing` is `Expr::Index` on stage 1 but `xs` plus stray statements on stage 2 — the engines disagree despite the report claiming they agree by construction, and no corpus or stage-2 test covers `at nothing` (the Rust-only test is tests/index_words_test.rs:390) — add the missing kinds to the bootstrap table and add a byte-identity case for `xs at nothing`.
2. [MAJOR] src/linter.rs:462 — `lint()` consults the analyzer only when errors and warnings are both empty, so an unrunnable file that also triggers any warning (e.g. `set u to unknown_name` with an unused name) reports only the warning and exits 0 via src/lib.rs:272 — `rb lint` stays green on a file `rb run` refuses, contradicting the claimed pairing — always run the analyzer and merge its refusal, and add a combined warning-plus-unknown-name test to settle it.
